rotless-skill-creator
Copyright 2026 rotless contributors

This skill is a modified version of Anthropic's skill-creator
(https://github.com/anthropics/skills/tree/main/skills/skill-creator, compared at
commit ca45fc496a3436251f191354091d557da31c15b5, forked from the newer copy distributed
with Claude), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE.txt).

Changes made by rotless contributors:
- SKILL.md: rewritten to work in any agent (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor, GitHub
  Copilot, OpenCode). It adds prior art through rotless-github-research, a failing-baseline step
  (an idea from obra/superpowers writing-skills, MIT), portability rules, three ways to run tests,
  a trigger-tuning loop the agent runs itself, and hand-offs to rotless-skill-modernizer and
  rotless-skill-refiner. The Claude app and Cowork sections are gone.
- scripts/run_eval.py: replaced. Trigger tests run on any agent CLI and detect that the skill
  loaded with a canary token, not Claude Code stream events.
- scripts/harness.py, scripts/run_case.py, scripts/make_eval_review.py, scripts/test_harness.py,
  agents/openai.yaml and assets/icon.svg: new.
- scripts/improve_description.py, scripts/run_loop.py and scripts/generate_report.py: removed.
  They needed `claude -p`; the agent now proposes descriptions itself (SKILL.md step 7).
- scripts/quick_validate.py: no PyYAML dependency; the name must match its folder; metadata
  must be a mapping; portability warnings.
- scripts/utils.py: UTF-8 file encoding; holds the one frontmatter parser that quick_validate.py
  and the runners share, which unescapes quoted YAML values.
- scripts/package_skill.py, scripts/aggregate_benchmark.py and eval-viewer/generate_review.py:
  UTF-8 file encoding (for Windows) and wording that doesn't assume one agent.
- agents/grader.md, agents/analyzer.md, agents/comparator.md and references/schemas.md: prose
  edited for plain style. Every instruction, field name, schema and example is unchanged.
- eval-viewer/generate_review.py: the server answers only its own page (an Origin and Host check, so
  another site can't write feedback.json), and it no longer kills whatever process holds its port.
- eval-viewer/viewer.html and assets/eval_review.html: system fonts instead of Google Fonts, and
  the two remaining lines that named Claude Code now say "your agent session".
- Comments and docstrings in scripts/package_skill.py, scripts/aggregate_benchmark.py,
  eval-viewer/generate_review.py and eval-viewer/viewer.html: edited for plain style, and the
  usage lines corrected. No code changed.

Unchanged from Anthropic's skill-creator: LICENSE.txt.
